   "id": 631718,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stem_html": "<p dir=\"ltr\">The plot below is a scatter plot of mean temperature in July and mean inches of rain per year for a sample of midwestern cities. A line is drawn to fit the data.&nbsp;</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><img alt=\"A SCATTER PLOT THAT SHOWS MEAN TEMPERATURE IN JULY IN DEGREES FAHRENHEIT ON THE X-AXIS AND MEAN RAINFALL PER YEAR IN INCHES ON THE Y-AXIS. THE LINE DRAWN INCREASES FROM LEFT TO RIGHT.\" class=\"img-fluid atto_image_button_text-bottom\" height=\"425\" src=\"exercises/media/f0b7af7afd40c04f.jpg\" width=\"450\"></p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Use the line provided to predict the mean number of inches of rain per year for a city that has a mean temperature of 70°F in July.&nbsp;<br></p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1222482,
     "content_html": "31.5 inches per year"
    },
    {
     "id": 1222481,
     "content_html": "34.5 inches per year"
    },
    {
     "id": 1222483,
     "content_html": "33.5 inches per year"
    },
    {
     "id": 1222480,
     "content_html": "32.5 inches per year"
    }
